module contract;

// CMetrics context release — resource-projection vocabulary version 1.
//
// Card W36-CORPUS-CONTRACTS-3. ONE TRUSTED ASSUMPTION about one upstream
// function. This module verifies nothing: the C body is not analyzed by this
// loader, and a declaration is a premise. Any verdict that rests on it is a
// verdict RELATIVE TO this declaration, never a proof of the C implementation.
//
// Read from the pinned checkout (`build/cycle19/fluent-bit-clang-source`) at
// Fluent Bit 66910c10a4d7eafa810b84229cf2dcf7b0f26f97 on this card's own run.
//
// ## Why this callee
//
// Three projected functions in the baseline are blocked by `cmt_destroy` and
// by nothing else — `cmt_decode_msgpack_destroy`
// (`lib/cmetrics/src/cmt_decode_msgpack.c:2204`),
// `cmt_decode_prometheus_remote_write_destroy` (`:895` of its own file) and
// `cmt_decode_statsd_destroy` (`:635`) — each holding exactly one leaf.
//
// ## `cmt_destroy`, read from `lib/cmetrics/src/cmetrics.c:92-146`
//
//     void cmt_destroy(struct cmt *cmt)
//     {
//         struct cfl_list *tmp;
//         struct cfl_list *head;
//         ...
//         cfl_list_foreach_safe(head, tmp, &cmt->counters) {
//             c = cfl_list_entry(head, struct cmt_counter, _head);
//             cmt_counter_destroy(c);
//         }
//         ... the same shape for gauges, summaries, histograms,
//             exp_histograms and untypeds ...
//         if (cmt->static_labels) {
//             cmt_labels_destroy(cmt->static_labels);
//         }
//         if (cmt->internal_metadata != NULL) {
//             cfl_kvlist_destroy(cmt->internal_metadata);
//         }
//         if (cmt->external_metadata != NULL) {
//             cfl_kvlist_destroy(cmt->external_metadata);
//         }
//         free(cmt);
//     }
//
//   * `cmt` is the ONLY parameter, and the LAST statement on every path is
//     `free(cmt)` — unconditional, not guarded, not on one arm. After the call
//     the caller may not read, write or release `cmt` again. That is what
//     `resource_released` says.
//   * The nullability marker is **`nonnull`**, and this is a measurement rather
//     than a default: the body has NO leading null guard. Its very first
//     executable statement dereferences the parameter —
//     `cfl_list_foreach_safe(head, tmp, &cmt->counters)` expands to a read of
//     `cmt->counters` — so `cmt_destroy(NULL)` is undefined behaviour upstream,
//     not a tolerated no-op. This is the opposite reading from the same card's
//     `cfl_sds_destroy` (`nullable`, whose first statement IS `if (!s) return;`)
//     and it is the reading `flb_input_chunk_destroy` already carries for the
//     same reason.
//   * The result is `void`, so `resource_return_none()` is the faithful — and
//     the only faithful — result mode.
//
// ## The cascade, stated rather than hidden
//
// The body releases far more than `cmt`: every counter, gauge, summary,
// histogram, exponential histogram and untyped on the context's six lists, the
// static labels, and both metadata kvlists. None of those is a tracked identity
// in this projection — they are reached only by walking `cmt`'s own intrusive
// lists, and no analysed call site in the corpus holds a separate binding to
// one. The declaration therefore states the custody fact about `cmt` and says
// NOTHING about the cascade; it does not assert that the cascade is complete,
// correct, or that it releases each member exactly once.
//
// ## ABI and modes (constraint 8)
//
// `lib/cmetrics/include/cmetrics/cmetrics.h:80` declares
//
//     void cmt_destroy(struct cmt *cmt);
//
// One object-pointer level — `ptr<mut, u8>` — and a `void` result, spelled
// `unit`. Arity one, matching every analysed call site; not variadic, so no
// `resource_variadic_data_tail()`.
//
// ## Declared although defined in a corpus unit
//
// `cmt_destroy` IS defined inside an audited unit, `cmetrics/cmetrics.c`, so
// unlike this card's `cfl_sds_destroy` it meets constraint 8's duty gate. Three
// things follow, and all three are deliberate. A declared contract always wins
// over an inferred W4 summary, and a disagreement is reported as a
// `SummaryConflict` diagnostic rather than silently resolved either way. A
// withdrawal, if the gate ever found a duty contradiction, would be scoped to
// **`cmetrics.c` alone** — the unit that defines the body — and the three call
// sites this declaration exists to decide are in three OTHER units, which
// define no body for it and so can derive no contradicting summary. And
// `cmetrics.c`'s own definition stays analyzable and is not rewritten.
//
// ## NOT CLAIMED
//
//   * Nothing about `cmt_counter_destroy`, `cmt_gauge_destroy`,
//     `cmt_summary_destroy`, `cmt_histogram_destroy`,
//     `cmt_exp_histogram_destroy`, `cmt_untyped_destroy`,
//     `cmt_labels_destroy` or `cfl_kvlist_destroy` — none is declared here.
//   * Nothing about whether a context reached this call in a valid state.
//   * Nothing about double release or use-after-free, which the gateway's own
//     liveness precondition refuses on settled denotations, unchanged here.
//   * Nothing about thread safety or ordering.

// --- the CMetrics context's release ----------------------------------------
extern fn cmt_destroy(cmt: ptr<mut, u8>) -> unit
contract {
    requires resource_contract_v1;
    ensures normal resource_released(cmt, nonnull);
    ensures normal resource_return_none();
};

// ## Card W45-CALLEE-CASCADE-RESIDUAL round 3: `cmt_atomic_initialize`
//
// ONE TRUSTED ASSUMPTION, pinned after reading every definition at both
// revisions. It is the only uncontracted call of `cmt_initialize`
// (`cmetrics.c:38-41`). The audited build compiles `cmt_atomic_clang.c`,
// whose definition (`:22-25`) is `return 0;`, and its body is Safe there (W4
// checks the declaration, rule 13g). The other platform definitions touch
// only file-scope state: `cmt_atomic_gcc.c:22-25` returns 0,
// `cmt_atomic_generic.c:45-54` runs `pthread_once` over its static bootstrap
// and reads a static status, and `cmt_atomic_msvc.c` defines it twice under
// `_WIN64`: one runs `InitOnceExecuteOnce` over its static bootstrap
// (`:52-63`), the other returns 0 (`:128-131`). No parameter, no custody:
// neutral.

extern fn cmt_atomic_initialize() -> i32
contract {
    requires resource_contract_v1;
    ensures normal resource_return_none();
};
